plit nearly evenly, and the midterm environment gives Bottoms a modest tailwind"], "rationale": "Every September survey gives Jackson a small lead and his overwhelming fundraising advantage is shaping the airwar, but expert ratings, a favorable environment, and even prediction markets keep Bottoms fully in the race. The evidence nets out to a razor-thin Republican edge in a genuine coin-flip.", "watch": "Whether Bottoms can close the advertising gap or capitalize on ticket-splitting voters, since a late polling shift in either direction would immediately flip the edge.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Brian Kemp (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Georgia's governor's race is an open-seat contest between Democrat Keisha Lance Bottoms and Republican Rick Jackson, and it sits near the top of the national map. Surveys from mid- and late September give Jackson a narrow one-to-three-point edge, though several of those pollsters lean Republican. Aggregated estimates range from a slight Democratic lead to a two-point Republican one, and prediction markets are split nearly evenly across platforms.\n\nMoney is the clearest asymmetry: Jackson has raised roughly $119 million to about $5.8 million for Bottoms, and news reports describe a steep Democratic advertising deficit. Expert raters overwhelmingly call the race a tossup, with two outlets leaning Democratic. The broader environment offers Bottoms a modest case, but the recent polling trend and the spending gap leave Jackson slightly favored in what remains a true tossup.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6414, "margin": 1.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5561, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5612, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5894, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5413, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5396, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5736, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem":